{"guid": "N60_001", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "fixture (sports)", "concept_definition": "In sports, a fixture is a match or game scheduled to take place on a particular date.", "translations": {"en": "fixture", "lt": "rungtynės", "zh": "赛程比赛", "fr": "rencontre programmée", "es": "partido programado", "es-419": "partido programado"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_002", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "match (sports)", "concept_definition": "A match in sports is a contest in which two players or teams compete against each other.", "translations": {"en": "match", "lt": "rungtynės", "zh": "比赛", "fr": "match", "es": "partido", "es-419": "partido"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_003", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "tournament (sports)", "concept_definition": "A tournament is an organized series of sports contests in which participants compete to determine a winner.", "translations": {"en": "tournament", "lt": "turnyras", "zh": "锦标赛", "fr": "tournoi", "es": "torneo", "es-419": "torneo"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_004", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "championship (sports)", "concept_definition": "A sports competition in which teams or players compete to determine who is the best.", "translations": {"en": "championship", "lt": "čempionatas", "zh": "锦标赛", "fr": "championnat", "es": "campeonato", "es-419": "campeonato"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_005", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "final (sports)", "concept_definition": "In sports, a final is the last match or contest in a competition, which decides the winner.", "translations": {"en": "final", "lt": "finalas", "zh": "决赛", "fr": "finale", "es": "final", "es-419": "final"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_006", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "semifinal (sports)", "concept_definition": "In a sports competition, a semifinal is one of the two matches that decide which competitors advance to the final.", "translations": {"en": "semifinal", "lt": "pusfinalis", "zh": "半决赛", "fr": "demi-finale", "es": "semifinal", "es-419": "semifinal"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_007", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "quarterfinal", "concept_definition": "A round in a sports tournament in which eight competitors or teams play matches, usually to decide which four advance to the semifinals.", "translations": {"en": "quarterfinal", "lt": "ketvirtfinalis", "zh": "四分之一决赛", "fr": "quart de finale", "es": "cuartos de final", "es-419": "cuartos de final"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_008", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "group stage", "concept_definition": "A part of a sports competition in which teams or players are divided into groups and play matches within their groups to decide who advances to the next stage.", "translations": {"en": "group stage", "lt": "grupės etapas", "zh": "小组赛阶段", "fr": "phase de groupes", "es": "fase de grupos", "es-419": "fase de grupos"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_009", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "upset (sports)", "concept_definition": "In sports, an upset is a win by a team or player expected to be weaker than the opponent.", "translations": {"en": "upset", "lt": "netikėta pergalė", "zh": "爆冷", "fr": "surprise", "es": "sorpresa", "es-419": "sorpresa"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_010", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "draw (sports)", "concept_definition": "In sports, a draw is a match that ends with both sides having the same score.", "translations": {"en": "draw", "lt": "lygiosios", "zh": "平局", "fr": "match nul", "es": "empate", "es-419": "empate"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_011", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "tie (sports)", "concept_definition": "In sports, an equal score between competitors or teams, so neither side is ahead; a tie may be the final result of a game or match.", "translations": {"en": "tie", "lt": "lygiosios", "zh": "平局", "fr": "match nul", "es": "empate", "es-419": "empate"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_012", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "tiebreak (sports)", "concept_definition": "A tiebreak is a method or extra period of play used in sports to decide the winner when the score is level.", "translations": {"en": "tiebreak", "lt": "lygiųjų nutraukimas", "zh": "决胜方式", "fr": "départage", "es": "desempate", "es-419": "desempate"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_013", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "kickoff (sports)", "concept_definition": "In sports, a kickoff is a kick that starts or restarts a match or period of play.", "translations": {"en": "kickoff", "lt": "pradinis smūgis", "zh": "开球", "fr": "coup d’envoi", "es": "saque inicial", "es-419": "saque inicial"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_014", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "overtime (sports)", "concept_definition": "In sports, overtime is extra playing time added when the score is tied at the end of regular time, to determine the winner or continue the game.", "translations": {"en": "overtime", "lt": "pratęsimas", "zh": "加时赛", "fr": "prolongation", "es": "tiempo extra", "es-419": "tiempo extra"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_015", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "timeout (sports)", "concept_definition": "In sports, a timeout is a short break in play requested by a team.", "translations": {"en": "timeout", "lt": "pertraukėlė", "zh": "暂停", "fr": "temps mort", "es": "tiempo muerto", "es-419": "tiempo fuera"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_016", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "foul (sports)", "concept_definition": "In sports, an action by a player that breaks the rules of the game.", "translations": {"en": "foul", "lt": "pražanga", "zh": "犯规", "fr": "faute", "es": "falta", "es-419": "falta"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N60_017", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "rule_defined_event", "concept_label": "save (sports)", "concept_definition": "In sports, a save is a goalkeeper's successful stop of a shot that would otherwise enter the goal.", "translations": {"en": "save", "lt": "atremtas smūgis", "zh": "扑救", "fr": "arrêt", "es": "parada", "es-419": "atajada"}, "difficulty_level": 405, "disambiguation": {"en": "sports"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
